From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <remora@localhost>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 08:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] statusbar: honor icon_blacklist in the Compose icon pipeline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The new_status_bar_icons aconfig flag is enabled in this build, which
routes system status icons through the Compose pipeline. That pipeline
filters icons by slot name in exactly one place — SystemStatusIconsViewModel
does `filterNot { it.slotName in blockedSlots }` — and the set it filters
against comes from SystemStatusIconBlocklistInteractor.

The home status bar's implementation only ever populated that set from the
config_collapsed_statusbar_icon_blocklist resource array plus the vibrate
icon setting. It never read Settings.Secure icon_blacklist, so the hide
list that the legacy status bar honored through TunerService silently
became a no-op for every migrated icon.

Read icon_blacklist here and union it into the blocked set. Slot names
survived the Compose migration unchanged (each SystemStatusIconViewModel
takes its slotName from the same com.android.internal.R.string.status_bar_*
tokens), so the existing hide list values keep working as-is.

The user list is additive: it can hide more slots, but cannot un-hide one
the device config blocked deliberately. Using the canonical icon_blacklist
key rather than a private one keeps `settings put secure icon_blacklist`
and third-party tuner apps working, and matches ConnectivityRepository,
which already reads the same key for the connectivity slots.
---
diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/pipeline/shared/domain/interactor/HomeStatusBarIconBlockListInteractor.kt b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/pipeline/shared/domain/interactor/HomeStatusBarIconBlockListInteractor.kt
index b1700a4f99b3..3618e16f1309 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/pipeline/shared/domain/interactor/HomeStatusBarIconBlockListInteractor.kt
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/pipeline/shared/domain/interactor/HomeStatusBarIconBlockListInteractor.kt
@@ -22,9 +22,11 @@ import com.android.systemui.dagger.SysUISingleton
 import com.android.systemui.dagger.qualifiers.Main
 import com.android.systemui.res.R
 import com.android.systemui.shared.settings.data.repository.SecureSettingsRepository
+import com.android.systemui.statusbar.phone.ui.StatusBarIconController
 import com.android.systemui.statusbar.systemstatusicons.domain.interactor.SystemStatusIconBlocklistInteractor
 import javax.inject.Inject
 import kotlinx.coroutines.flow.Flow
+import kotlinx.coroutines.flow.combine
 import kotlinx.coroutines.flow.map
 
 /** A place to define the blocklist/allowlist for home status bar icons */
@@ -42,18 +44,39 @@ constructor(@Main res: Resources, secureSettingsRepository: SecureSettingsReposi
     private val shouldShowVibrateIcon: Flow<Boolean> =
         secureSettingsRepository.boolSetting(Settings.Secure.STATUS_BAR_SHOW_VIBRATE_ICON, false)
 
+    /**
+     * Tracks the user's status bar icon hide list.
+     *
+     * This is the same `icon_blacklist` secure setting the legacy (pre-Compose) status bar honored
+     * through TunerService, and which [ConnectivityRepository] still reads for the connectivity
+     * slots. Reading it here re-attaches it to the Compose icon pipeline, whose only per-slot
+     * filter is [SystemStatusIconsViewModel]'s `filterNot { it.slotName in blockedSlots }`.
+     */
+    private val userBlockedIcons: Flow<Set<String>> =
+        secureSettingsRepository.stringSetting(StatusBarIconController.ICON_HIDE_LIST).map {
+            hideList ->
+            hideList
+                ?.split(',')
+                ?.map { slot -> slot.trim() }
+                ?.filter { slot -> slot.isNotEmpty() }
+                ?.toSet()
+                .orEmpty()
+        }
+
     override val blockedIconSlots: Flow<Set<String>> =
-        shouldShowVibrateIcon.map {
+        combine(shouldShowVibrateIcon, userBlockedIcons) { showVibrateIcon, userBlocked ->
             val defaultSet = defaultBlockedIcons.toMutableSet()
             // It's possible that the vibrate icon was in the default blocklist, so we manually
             // merge the setting and list
-            if (it) {
+            if (showVibrateIcon) {
                 defaultSet.remove(vibrateIconSlot)
             } else {
                 defaultSet.add(vibrateIconSlot)
             }
 
-            defaultSet
+            // The user's hide list is additive: it can only ever hide more, never un-hide a slot
+            // the device config blocked on purpose.
+            defaultSet + userBlocked
         }
 
     val iconBlockList: Flow<List<String>> = blockedIconSlots.map { it.toList() }
